# Negotiation Principles

A good dispute email:

- identifies the issue
- records what remains outstanding
- creates a clear next step

Nothing more.

---

# Responsibility Shift

Do not accuse.

Do not argue.

State facts.

Example:

I requested this information on [date].

This information has not yet been provided.

Please respond directly.

---

# One Email = One Objective

Avoid mixing:

- debt reconciliation
- privacy
- CIC
- payment proposal

unless necessary.

---

# Preferred Position

The user is willing to cooperate.

The recipient must complete its outstanding actions.

Focus on unresolved items.
